    "NT_VERSE_REF": "Philippians 2:11",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "And every tongue confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Deuteronomy 6:4 — “Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God, the LORD is one.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "Philippians 2:11 — “And every tongue confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.”",
    "GREEK": "Κύριος",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "Kyrios",
    "HEBREW": "יְהוָה",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "Yahweh",
    "OT_REFS": "Ex 3:14 • 1 Sam 2:7 • Ps 23:1 • Isa 6:1 • Job 1:21",
    "NT_REFS": "Matt 22:44 • Luke 6:46 • Acts 2:36 • Rom 10:9 • Rev 19:16",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "In English Bibles, 'LORD' (small caps) represents the Hebrew name Yahweh.",
      "The Greek 'Kyrios' was used by the Septuagint to translate the divine name.",
